Chapter: Fat32FsinfoHint

  cites Foreword chapter Fat32
  cites Foreword chapter Fat16

 FSInfo's next-free field is a hint the medium supplies. A FAT32 volume
 formatted at sector 2048 for 20480 sectors has its hint rewritten to
 268435440, past every cluster the volume has; the hint must read as unknown,
 so a file still writes on a free volume. A hint inside the volume is kept.

Section: Helpers

  set-hint : Integer -> [Device.Block] Integer
  set-hint (v) = act
    fs <- block-read-sector 2049
    let w = fat32-fmt-u32 fs 492 v
    in block-write-sector 2049 fs
  end

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (v) = if v then "yes" else "no"

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Device.Block] Nothing = act
    fmt <- fat32-format 2048 20480 "CODEX"
    h1 <- set-hint 268435440
    vol <- fat32-init 2048
    w <- fat32-write-file vol "A.TXT" [1, 2, 3]
    print-line-uni ("past hint: next-free " & show (vol.f32-next-free) & " write " & yn w)
    h2 <- set-hint 100
    vol2 <- fat32-init 2048
    print-line-uni ("inside hint: next-free " & show (vol2.f32-next-free))
  end
